 "notes": "Shag Rock, a reef about 1 km across at the eastern edge of the Strait of Gubal, outline from OpenStreetMap. The Kingston lies on its western tip (Red Sea Wreck Project position); the reef dive drifts from there along the southern wall with the reef on the left shoulder to a zodiac pick-up. The sandy plateau at 8-10 m with a permanent mooring is not placed because its position is unknown; drift direction depends on the current.",
